cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference FocusFlow, please cite it as below."
title: "FocusFlow: Open-Source App Blocker and Focus Planner for Android"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TBTechs"
    website: "https://tbtechs.pages.dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TITANICBHAI/FocusFlow"
url: "https://focusflowapp.pages.dev/"
abstract: >-
  FocusFlow is a free, open-source Android app that blocks distracting apps and
  helps plan focused work. It uses Android's Accessibility Service, an optional
  on-device VPN and optional Device Admin protection, and is built natively with
  Kotlin and Jetpack Compose. Data stays on the device.
keywords:
  - android
  - app blocker
  - focus
  - productivity
  - digital wellbeing
  - screen time
  - kotlin
  - jetpack compose
  - open source
